algorithms.pseudocode:
Algorithm: ClassifyMonsterTriples(b, N)
Input: base b >= 2, bound N
Output: list of (kind, v, x, y) tuples

for v = 4 to N:
    for x = 2 to sqrt(v):
        if x does not divide v: continue
        y = v / x
        if y < x: continue
        // Modular sieve (Theorem 1): O(1) check
        if (x*y) mod (b-1) != (x+y) mod (b-1): continue
        // Full digit-bag check: O(log_b(v))
        if digitBag_b(v) = digitBag_b(x) + digitBag_b(y):
            emit (vampire, v, x, y)
        elif digitOverlap_b(v,x) = 0 and digitOverlap_b(v,y) = 0:
            emit (ghost, v, x, y)

Time: O(N^{3/2} * log_b(N))
Space: O(N) for results
Sieve eliminates ~92% of candidates in base 10.
